# Every text file checks out with LF, Windows included. Git for Windows' default
# (`core.autocrlf=true`) would otherwise hand a Windows checkout CRLF text, and
# whatever the build embeds or a test compares byte-for-byte breaks there only:
# blessed snapshots (#1036), the game `CLAUDE.md` template `include_str!` reads
# (#1345). Binary files are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
